SUMMARY:Mozart's Il Don Giovanni: Talk and Performance
DESCRIPTION:\n\n\nNote: This is a paid Adult School class. Click here to 
 register.\n\n"I have an inexpressible desire to write an opera 
 again"--Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart\n\nJoin another one of our popular two-part 
 cultural classes to experience the impassioned genius that Mozart brought 
 to his favorite medium:\n\nTuesday\, July 7: Come to Montclair Public 
 Library to learn all about Mozart's operas from Sarah Sweeney\, a singer 
 and scholar of musicology from Montclair State University\n\nSaturday\, 
 July 11: Drive yourself to the Alexander Kasser Theater at Montclair State 
 University for a full performance of Il Don Giovanni\, one of his most 
 celebrated works\, performed by the renowned company\, Teatro Nuovo. The 
 event will also include a brief pre-concert and a free talk on Don Giovanni 
 itself by legendary Teatro Nuovo artistic director Will Crutchfield. \n
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Conference Room\, Montclair Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Adult School":MAILTO:adultschool@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Adult School, Lectures / History & Culture, Music
