SUMMARY:Everything Book Club\, "To the Lighthouse" by Virginia Woolf (New Session)
DESCRIPTION:After we read "1984\," you asked for more classics so here we 
 are! \n\nIn this masterpiece of modernist literature\, the Ramsay family\, 
 along with a group of their friends and guests\, gather at their summer 
 home on the Scottish coast\, anticipating a long-promised trip to the 
 lighthouse across the bay. In part one\, the action revolves around Mrs. 
 Ramsay. In part two\, the family returns without her. If you've always 
 meant to read this book\, now's your chance! If you've read it before\, 
 let's explore it again together.\n\n"I read this book like I eat 
 chocolate\, always intending to indulge in just a little bit\, then finding 
 myself inexorably unwilling to stop."—The Guardian\n\nBorn in 1882\, 
 Virginia Woolf is recognized as a major 20th-century author\, a great 
 novelist and essayist and a key figure in literary history. With her 
 sister\, the painter Vanessa Bell\, she was drawn into the company of 
 writers and artists later known as the Bloomsbury Group. Woolf struggled 
 with mental illness all of her life and in 1941\, fearing another attack\, 
 she drowned herself.\n\n
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Teen Room\, Montclair Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Library":MAILTO:events@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Adult Services, Book Discussion
UID:LibCal-10306-17088653
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/17088653
END:VEVENT
