SUMMARY:A Deep Dive into the Desegregation of Montclair's Pools: A Panel Discussion
DESCRIPTION:Note: Click below to register or on the Adult School 
 Website.\n\n A free Adult School/Adult Services local history discussion. 
 Co-presented by The Montclair History Center. \n\n Let's explore the story 
 of Montclair's three public pools: why they were built\, how they became 
 available to residents of all races--and how they fit into the history of 
 civil rights and desegregation as a whole. \n\nModerated by Dionne Ford 
 ("Go Back and Get It"). With Lonnie Brandon\, former longtime director of 
 Montclair's Parks and Recreation and Angelica Diggs\, director of the 
 Montclair History Center. \n\nThis is a free event but registration is 
 required.
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Auditorium\, Montclair Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Adult School":MAILTO:adultschool@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Adult School, Adult Services, Special Event
UID:LibCal-10306-16929382
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/16929382
