SUMMARY:MCP Server with Fabric (Power BI and data agents)
DESCRIPTION:Cloud Data Driven\nIn this session\, I explore how the Model C
 ontext Protocol (MCP) enables a new way for AI agents to securely and inte
 lligently interact with Microsoft Fabric.\n\nYou’ll see how MCP servers 
 expose Power BI semantic models and Fabric data agents as discoverable too
 ls\, allowing agents to reason over enterprise data\, query it in natural 
 language\, act on top of it and edit semantic models for Power BI.\n\nI wi
 ll walk through real scenarios where data agents and Power BI models becom
 e first-class citizens in agent workflows\, unlocking more contextual\, tr
 ustworthy\, and scalable AI experiences across the Fabric ecosystem.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/cloud-data-driven/events/315353906/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260621T140747Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260621T140747Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Montclairfoundation Calendar Of Events": "https://montclairfoundation.org/event/summer-at-van-vleck-seasonal-interest-summer-tour/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:montclairfoundation_calendar_of_events
X-SOURCE:Montclair Foundation
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260723T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260723T143000
DTSTAMP:20260624T001652
CREATED:20260609T221802Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260610T214433Z
UID:10007681-1784813400-1784817000@montclairfoundation.org
SUMMARY:Summer at Van Vleck - Seasonal Interest Summer Tour
DESCRIPTION:Partner Program with the Montclair Institute for Lifelong Learning \nThursdays\, July 16 – Aug 20\, 1:30 PM – 2:30 PM \nJuly 23 – Seasonal Interest Summer Tour – Join Laura Roberts\, Director of Horticulture at The Montclair Foundation – Van Vleck House & Gardens\, for a journey through the beauty of the season. Tour highlights will include many beautiful blooming specimens as well as a visit to our Kitchen Garden which showcases a bountiful collection of veggies\, greens\, and herbs. Outdoor tour\, so please dress for the weather with appropriate footwear. \nJuly 30 – Collage Art – Unplug and make something unexpectedly beautiful.  In this hands-on collage class\, we’ll be using natural materials from the Gardens\, and turn them into your personal masterpiece. Learn about composition\, texture\, color and layering\, while using leaves\, petals\, moss\, bark seed and other found objects.  No art experience needed – just curiosity and desire to play and turn found objects into a one-of-a-kind piece of art to treasure. \nAug 6 – Qigong – Through careful balancing forms and gentle breath awareness\, you’ll connect to your body’s wisdom in the natural beauty of the Van Vleck garden. \nNo experience necessary; bring a yoga mat or towel and an open mind. Instructor: Jodi Brooks. \nAug 13 – Drought Resistant Plants – Join us for a walking tour of the drought resistant plants thriving in the gardens of Van Vleck and learn why they are so tolerant of our New Jersey summers. Instructor: Laura Roberts\, Director of Horticulture \nAug 20 – Guided Nature Walk  – Spend an afternoon in the gardens of Van Vleck with Volunteer Naturalist Jenny Aley. Search for birds and other animals\, as well as the signs they leave behind. Learn interesting facts and information about the wildlife we share our backyards with.  \nThis class is a Partner Program with the Montclair Institute for Lifelong Learning. To register please visit: http://schedulesplus.com/montclair/kiosk
URL:https://montclairfoundation.org/event/summer-at-van-vleck-seasonal-interest-summer-tour/
LOCATION:Van Vleck House & Gardens\, 21 Van Vleck Street\, Montclair\, 07042\, United States
CATEGORIES:Classes,Adults
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://montclairfoundation.org/content/uploads/2022/04/default.jpg
END:VEVENT
